  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "fh_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -314
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Flock Herder\n\nHold the mouse button down and the flock streams towards the pointer; let go and they go back to flocking on their own. F turns the lure into a scare: held, the birds flee the pointer instead. Keys 1, 2, 3 change the flock's character — 1 a loose drift, 2 a tight school, 3 a nervous swarm — and S scatters it afresh. The sliders still tune separation, alignment and cohesion on top.\n\nHow it works: the Simulation node's flocking mode does the boids; the pointer is its `target` and `attract` is +, − or 0 depending on the button and F (a Latch). The characters are three columns of numbers picked by a key with Lookup. Connect Points draws the lines between near neighbours, and Echo leaves fading trails.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 250
      }
    },
